          a: `Honestly: **not well enough to be useful for prediction.**\n\n- Only **58 countries** had complete data for every indicator, leaving **18** for testing.\n- **Regression** (predicting the rate itself) failed on unseen countries: test R² was −0.36 (linear), −0.60 (decision tree) and 0.13 (SVR).\n- **Classification** (above/below 11.5 per 100k): the best models, a linear SVM and a tuned random forest, scored **72%** on the test set, but always guessing "low" scores **61%**, and cross-validated accuracy varied by ±18–24 points.\n\nThe value of the exercise is the lesson: with so few countries and so much missing data, the indicators can describe patterns but can't reliably predict.`,
